title: duplicates panel
tags: Panel Duplicates
kind: reference
summary: The repository's duplicate groups, worst reclaimable space first, to expand and to delete copies from.

Open it with `panel:open here duplicates` (<<key "panel:open here duplicates" "t u">>).
The groups are listed collapsed, worst reclaimable space first: reclaimable
space, file size, number of copies, hash. The ''Scan'' button runs
`mf:duplicate scan` ([[Finding duplicates]]).

* <<key "duplicates:activate other" Enter>>, <<key "duplicates:toggle-group" →>> or the group's `▸`/`▾` button — expand a group into its members' paths; a `+` marks a member that shares an inode with another (a hard link: removing it frees nothing).
* <<key "duplicates:activate other" Enter>> on a member, or its `↗` button ([[Opening a row]]) — show it in the [[viewer panel]] of the other slot; <<key "panel:open other metarecord-detail" Shift+Enter>> or `ⓘ` — in the [[metarecord-detail panel]] (on a group row: the group's own metarecord). The row under the cursor is the selection, so a viewer panel beside the list follows it.
* <<key "cursor:find self select" f>> — jump to a group by hash, or to a copy by path ([[Jumping to an entry]]).
* <<key "cursor:next self" "↓">> / <<key "cursor:prev self" "↑">>, <<key "cursor:first self" Home>> / <<key "cursor:last self" End>> — move; <<key "view:refresh self" "Ctrl+r">> — reload.
* <<key "duplicates:keep" "p k">> — keep the copy under the cursor, trash the others; <<key "item:delete" Delete>> — trash that copy alone, or on a group row delete the group's metarecord ([[Deleting duplicate copies]]).

Moving the cursor publishes the row as the workspace's selection: on a member row,
the file's metarecord; on a header row, the group's own metarecord (its hash,
size and counters are its fields, readable in the detail panel). So the shared
file actions and the detail panel follow the cursor.
